<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whether it’s gnawed electrical wires, droppings in cupboards, or foul odours from hidden nests, rodents pose risks that no home or workplace can afford to ignore.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This blog aims to help Melbourne homeowners identify the three most common types of rodents found in local properties and understand why professional </span><b>Melbourne rodent control</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> from</span><a href="/rodent-control-in-melbourne/"> <span style="font-weight: 400;">7 States Pest Control</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> is the safest and most effective way to eliminate them.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Why Melbourne Faces a Rodent Problem</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Melbourne’s mix of dense housing, mild climate, and thriving urban layout creates a perfect environment for rodents to survive and multiply. With its network of drainage systems, old buildings, and abundant food sources, the city offers rodents everything they need — warmth, shelter, and food access.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Rodents are highly adaptable creatures. They can enter homes and commercial spaces through:</span></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cracks and gaps in walls or floors</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Roof openings and ceiling cavities</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Drains, vents, or damaged pipes</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Poorly sealed doors, windows, and garage areas</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Seasonal changes also play a major role. During </span><b>Melbourne’s colder months</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">, rodents seek indoor shelter to stay warm. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once they find a safe space, they build nests, reproduce rapidly, and can turn a minor problem into a major infestation in a short time.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Without timely intervention, rodents can cause expensive property damage and create serious hygiene risks. That’s why prevention and professional inspection are essential for long-term rodent control.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">The 3 Most Common Rodents Found in Melbourne Homes</span></h3>
<ol>
<li><b> House Mice<br/>
<img alt="melbourne rodent control
" class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-9642" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" height="300" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" src="/storage/cms/blog/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-04-at-3.31.21-PM-300x300_3c7e0899.jpeg" srcset="/storage/cms/blog/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-04-at-3.31.21-PM-300x300_3c7e0899.jpeg 300w, /storage/cms/blog/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-04-at-3.31.21-PM-150x150_47648435.jpeg 150w, /storage/cms/blog/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-04-at-3.31.21-PM-768x768_be5dc5e6.jpeg 768w, /storage/cms/blog/WhatsApp-Image-2025-11-04-at-3.31.21-PM_9d03f6bc.jpeg 1024w" width="300"/></b></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">House mice are the smallest yet most common rodents found across Melbourne. They are extremely agile and can squeeze through openings as small as a coin. These pests often hide in kitchens, pantries, or storage rooms where food is accessible.</span></p>
<p><b>Characteristics:</b></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Size: Around 7–10 cm with a thin tail</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Colour: Light brown to grey</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Preferred areas: Warm indoor spaces near food sources</span></li>
</ul>
<p><b>Habits and Risks:</b><b><br/>
</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">House mice reproduce rapidly — one pair can produce dozens of offspring within a few months. Common signs of infestation include small droppings, gnaw marks on food packaging, shredded paper or cloth for nesting, and scratching noises at night.</span></p>
<p><b>They pose several risks:</b></p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Food contamination:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Mice spread bacteria such as Salmonella and Listeria.</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Property damage:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> They gnaw on wires and furniture, leading to fire hazards.</span></li>
<li aria-level="1" style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Health threats:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Their droppings and urine trigger allergies and asthma.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Due to their fast breeding cycle, early detection and professional treatment are critical to prevent large infestations.</span></p>
